   - Creates a **refresh token** with `sub`, `iat`, `exp`, and `typ: "refresh"`, using a 7-day TTL in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:9) and [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:18).
   - Signs both tokens with `SECRET` and `HS256`, defined in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:6) and [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:7).
   - Returns `{"access": access, "refresh": refresh}` in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:22).

2. `validate(token)`
   - Decodes the token using the shared `SECRET` and allowed algorithm list `[ALGO]` in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:28).
   - PyJWT verifies the signature and `exp` during decode. If the token is expired, it catches `ExpiredSignatureError` and returns `None` in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:29).
   - If the token is otherwise malformed, signed with the wrong secret, uses an unacceptable algorithm, or fails another JWT validation rule, it catches `InvalidTokenError` and returns `None` in [auth/jwt.py](/Users/basethesis/Desktop/benchmark_hermes-fabric/prereqs%202/fixtures/task01_explain_jwt/auth/jwt.py:31).
